created: 2025-05-29, last updated: 2026-04-16, [Read more](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/issues/4563)

Now, with Zod 3 and its zod-to-json-schema package, all intersections are flattened together (as shown in the examples).
However, in Zod 4, each parent intersection encapsulates the child one, causing a lot of nesting in the outputted schema.
...
```
import { z } from "zod"; // or "zod/v4"
import { zodToJsonSchema } from "zod-to-json-schema"
...
// Zod 3
console.log(JSON.stringify(zodToJsonSchema(HelloSchema), null, 2))
// Zod 4
console.log(JSON.stringify(z.toJSONSchema(HelloSchema, { target: "draft-7" }), null, 2))
```
